  psubq-xmm : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  psubq-xmm (dst) (src) =
   [102, 15, 251, modrm 3 dst src]

 The GPR here is the ModRM.reg field, so a destination in R8-R15 needs
 REX.R, and the XMM is the rm field, so REX.B. This carried no REX byte at
 all until 2026-07-27, and modrm masks its operands to three bits, so
 movmskpd into R11 silently encoded RBX. alloc-temp rotates
 [RAX, RCX, RDX, RSI, RDI, R11] and R11 is the only extended register in
 that pool, so about one mask query in six wrote its bits to RBX while the
 test-rr that follows -- which does emit REX -- read R11. The two named
 different registers, sete answered from whatever R11 held, and the query
 returned a wrong Boolean with no diagnostic. It also clobbered RBX, a
 callee-saved local register.

  movmskpd : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  movmskpd (gpr) (xmm) =
   if (gpr >= 8) | (xmm >= 8)
   then [102, rex False (gpr >= 8) False (xmm >= 8), 15, 80, modrm 3 gpr xmm]
   else [102, 15, 80, modrm 3 gpr xmm]

  unpcklpd-xmm : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  unpcklpd-xmm (dst) (src) =
   [102, 15, 20, modrm 3 dst src]

